# Scenario 'boot_states': what the boot does with damaged or unusual saved data. Every attempt changes the save RAM or the adapter's EEPROM
# image with the runtime directives `sram B:ADDR=VV`, `sramfill VV`, `cfg OFF=VV`, `cfgfill VV`, then power-cycles (`reset`) and looks at the
# screens for ~1400 frames (title / registration / error screens; two A presses each). The attempts are cumulative (a repaired save stays repaired).
# Known integrity code (docs/research/sram_layout.md section 2): bank 0 pages A000-AFFE / B000-BFFE with sums at AFFE / BFFE (22:4EF0-4FDE: repair from the
# valid page, else clear both), bank 1 sums at A8D7, A8B5, A9E4/A9E8 and page B000, bank 2 = copy of the adapter's 192-byte config (sum at A0BE).
# Adapter config: 'MA' magic, big-endian byte sum at BE-BF (libmobile config verify). Starts from the state left by 'tutorial_profile'.
# --- control
reset
wait 1000
shot control_boot
tap A
waitstable 60 max 600
shot control_a1
tap A
waitstable 60 max 600
shot control_a2
# --- bank0_page0
sram 0:A010=5A
sram 0:A011=A5
reset
wait 1000
shot bank0_page0_boot
tap A
waitstable 60 max 600
shot bank0_page0_a1
tap A
waitstable 60 max 600
shot bank0_page0_a2
# --- bank0_page1
sram 0:B010=5A
sram 0:B011=A5
reset
wait 1000
shot bank0_page1_boot
tap A
waitstable 60 max 600
shot bank0_page1_a1
tap A
waitstable 60 max 600
shot bank0_page1_a2
# --- bank0_both
sram 0:A010=5A
sram 0:A011=A5
sram 0:B010=5A
sram 0:B011=A5
reset
wait 1000
shot bank0_both_boot
tap A
waitstable 60 max 600
shot bank0_both_a1
tap A
waitstable 60 max 600
shot bank0_both_a2
# --- bank1_A100
sram 1:A100=5A
sram 1:A101=A5
reset
wait 1000
shot bank1_A100_boot
tap A
waitstable 60 max 600
shot bank1_A100_a1
tap A
waitstable 60 max 600
shot bank1_A100_a2
# --- bank1_A690
sram 1:A690=5A
sram 1:A691=A5
reset
wait 1000
shot bank1_A690_boot
tap A
waitstable 60 max 600
shot bank1_A690_a1
tap A
waitstable 60 max 600
shot bank1_A690_a2
# --- bank1_B010
sram 1:B010=5A
sram 1:B011=A5
reset
wait 1000
